# Lego pipeline — agent workflow

## Goals

Green only when: **1 clutch section**, **0 AABB collisions**, **hollow**. Tip-over is deferred.

Soft (not a gate): clutch `weak_edges` / `mean_overlap` from `connectivity.clutch_strength` — improve in a separate session on already-PASS models; never solid-fill to chase it.

## One writer

- At most **one** agent edits reconnect/collision code at a time.
- Optional second agent: explore or review only — no parallel edits to `phase5/plate_bridge.py`.

## One gap per session

- Name a single success metric (e.g. keep diameter 16 PASS; fix exhaust at 5 sections).
- Do not mix visual polish, staple budget, and scale in one run.

## Baseline lock

- Default demo diameter is **16** (`BASELINE_DIAMETER_STUDS`).
- Do not raise the default until that size stays PASS.
- Scale 18/20+ only after current size is green; keep experiments off the locked default.

## Visual polish / clutch strength

- Separate chat/session only.
- Only on already-PASS exports — do not change reconnect ordering in a polish session.

## Verify

Always end with `python -m phase5.demo_sphere` and report sections + collisions + parts + weak_edges/mean_overlap.
Paste reconnect log snippets on FAIL.
